    32	`bind_provenance.py --runs DIR ... --attempt FINAL ... --audit JSON --results JSON ...
    33	--rendered FILE ... --unseen-table JSON --unseen-binding JSON [--approved JSON] --out
    34	REPORT_DIRECTORY` validates the completion links and exclusively creates
    35	`binding_report_<UTC timestamp>.json` in that existing directory. It binds the three
    36	attempts with their inventory sidecar, probe receipt and hours ledger (at most one retry per
    37	arm), the released checkpoint at its pinned digest, the forty seen runs with their
    38	`seen_split` bindings and training linkage, the alignment audit, the four producer outputs
    39	with their sidecars and companions, the rendered documents (each must cite every canonical
    40	digest), the exp_04 table, sidecar and binding report, the approval blob and git HEAD.
    41	`check_record.py REPORT_DIRECTORY` recomputes the latest report under its own recorded HEAD;
    42	an invalid latest report fails with no fallback.
    43	
    44	Order of operations:
    45	
    46	1. Finish and review the code, then commit it. Compute the producer closures from that
    47	   committed code, fill every closure and checkpoint pin together, and commit the approval
    48	   file in a second reviewed commit before running any producer. The schema permits only
    49	   all-null or all-filled pins.
    50	2. Run `tools/exp07_table.py` once and `tools/exp07_pairs.py` once per registered pairing.
    51	   Keep each JSON, its sidecar and its companion (the living Markdown table, the pairing
    52	   summary) together.
    53	3. Run `bind_provenance.py` over the complete run set and all four canonical JSONs, then
    54	   `check_record.py`.
    55	4. Generate the Markdown, HTML and LaTeX from the bound JSONs, bind again so the report
    56	   covers the published documents, and run `check_record.py` once more before publication.
    57	
    58	Run `bash static_checks.sh` from this directory or by its full path: it compiles the assets
    59	and the exp_07 producers, checks whitespace, and runs the exp_07 suite plus the record-tool
    60	tests in both collection orders (exp_03, exp_04 and exp_07 ship files of the same name, so
    61	each experiment loads its own by path under its own `sys.modules` key).

