Rounds are closed per the SOP (review → fixes → re-verification → notebook entry); a final integrative Codex review (`seen_protocol_codex_code_full_review.md`) precedes the first probe. The deferred GPU parity (round 1) runs the moment a GPU is free and must pass before any launch. Pin-finalisation sequence (after the three trainings): pin the three checkpoint sha256 → compute closures at the fill HEAD → fill the JSON → single commit → producers; a missing or unapproved pin refuses production (exploratory mode lists it). The record binds the three probe receipts, the parity/calibration/audit evidence, every attempt including aborted ones, and asserts the one-retry maximum per arm from the ledgers.

